## 4. Credit-Based Billing System

### Pricing Model

- **Base:** $250/month per agent (Stripe subscription, quantity-based)
- **Included credits:** 50,000 tokens per agent per month
- **Overage:** billed at end of cycle via Stripe Metered Billing
- **Landing page hosting:** separate MRR line item per workspace

### Plan Tiers

| Plan | Agents | Included Credits | Price/mo |
|---|---|---|---|
| Starter | 1 | 50K tokens | $250 |
| Growth | 3 | 150K tokens | $650 |
| Pro | 5 | 250K tokens | $999 |
| Custom | 1–10 | Negotiated | Custom |

### Stripe Setup

**Product 1 — Agent Subscription**
- Recurring, $250/unit/month, quantity = agent_count
- Update via: `stripe.subscriptions.update({ items: [{ id, quantity }] })`

**Product 2 — Credit Overage (Metered)**
- Recurring, metered, aggregated sum
- Price: $0.10 per 1,000 overage tokens
- Report via Stripe Billing Meters: `stripe.billing.meterEvents.create({ event_name, payload: { stripe_customer_id, value } })`

**Product 3 — Landing Page Hosting**
- Recurring flat rate, separate subscription item per workspace

### Usage Logging Flow

Every OpenRouter call in `hermes-sidecar` or any agent route must call `lib/billing/logUsage.ts`:

```typescript
// lib/billing/logUsage.ts
export async function logAgentUsage({
  workspaceId,
  agentId,
  userId,
  model,
  usage,   // { prompt_tokens, completion_tokens }
  costUsd
}: LogUsageParams) {
  const totalTokens = usage.prompt_tokens + usage.completion_tokens
  
  await supabaseAdmin.from('credit_usage_events').insert({
    workspace_id: workspaceId,
    agent_id: agentId,
    user_id: userId,
    model,
    prompt_tokens: usage.prompt_tokens,
    completion_tokens: usage.completion_tokens,
    total_tokens: totalTokens,
    cost_usd: costUsd,
  })
  
  await reportToStripeMetered(workspaceId, totalTokens)
}
```

