## 5. Workspace Settings Tab

Lives at `/app/workspaces/[id]/settings` and `/app/admin/(dashboard)/workspaces/[id]/settings`.

Inspired by the Intraplex demo (clearance levels, siloed teams, simplified mode for non-technical clients).

### 5.1 Tab: General

**Workspace Admin sees:**
- Workspace name, logo, primary color
- Language (ES / EN)
- Timezone
- Subdomain (read-only)

**Super Admin additionally:**
- Internal notes (private)
- Stripe customer ID (link)
- "Suspend Workspace" toggle
- Linked intake submission

### 5.2 Tab: Members & Roles

Uses existing `workspace_members` table with roles `admin | operator | viewer`.

| Role | Permissions |
|---|---|
| Admin | Full workspace access, invite, settings |
| Operator | Use agents, view data, no settings |
| Viewer | Read-only dashboards/reports |

**Actions:** invite by email (Supabase magic link), change role, remove member, resend/cancel pending invites.

**Super Admin additionally:** "Login as user" impersonation, force-remove, see login timestamps.

### 5.3 Tab: Clearance & Permissions (Key New Feature)

**Clearance Levels (per user):**

| Level | Name | Access |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Public | General info, landing page data |
| 2 | Internal | Agent conversations, basic reports |
| 3 | Confidential | Full CRM, all records |
| 4 | Restricted | Integrations + billing + everything |

Each data object, agent, or view gets a minimum clearance requirement. Users below that level see nothing (completely hidden).

**Feature Flags (Super Admin controls per workspace):**
- `can_use_agents`
- `can_view_billing`
- `can_invite_members`
- `can_create_automations`
- `can_export_data`
- `can_access_connectors`
- `simplified_mode` (hides advanced UI)
- `max_members`
- `max_agents`

**Workspace Admin scoped controls:**
- Per-member sidebar visibility toggles
- Per-agent user access
- Simplified Mode toggle for non-technical team members

### 5.4 Tab: Agent Controls

**Workspace Admin:**
- List agents, toggle on/off, edit name/description
- Set which users can interact with each agent (clearance-based)

**Super Admin additionally:**
- Change model per agent (cost management)
- Set max tokens per agent per day
- Enable/disable agent skills
- Deploy new agent button
- View container name + droplet assignment

### 5.5 Tab: Data & Connectors

**Workspace Admin** (if `can_access_connectors = true`):
- Connected sources list
- Add connector (simplified wizard or advanced)
- Knowledge bases
- Disconnect/re-sync

**Super Admin additionally:**
- Raw connector config (vault-stored credentials)
- Connection health + error logs
- Storage usage

**Simplified Mode:** only shows "Connected Files" upload + list. No DB connectors.

### 5.6 Tab: Appearance
Brand colors, logo, language, landing page preview, custom domain (Pro plan only).

### 5.7 Tab: Audit Log

**Workspace Admin sees:**
- Chronological log: user, action, timestamp, resource
- Risk level badge (Low/Medium/High)
- Filter by user, date, action type
- CSV export

**Super Admin additionally:** cross-workspace audit view, flag entries.

### 5.8 Tab: Billing & Plan (Super Admin Only)
Plan tier, MRR, credit usage meter, Stripe subscription status, add/remove agents, change plan, cancel with grace period.

